-- Migration 0027 (docs/plans/schema-hardening.md). Generated by drizzle-kit, then HAND-EDITED into the order below. drizzle's migrator
-- runs the whole file in ONE transaction, so SET LOCAL lasts exactly this migration and a failure rolls everything back.
-- Order: lock timeout; drop the publishable CHECK; add columns nullable; create the table; backfill; SET NOT NULL; re-add the publishable
-- CHECK; new NOT VALID CHECKs; indexes; triggers LAST (a trigger earlier would refuse the backfills).
-- Backfill policy: where the true actor or time of an old row is unknown the sentinel 'system:pre-0027' is written, never a guess.

-- Hand edit: fail fast instead of queueing behind a long transaction while holding ACCESS EXCLUSIVE locks.
SET LOCAL lock_timeout = '5s';--> statement-breakpoint

-- Hand edit: media_versions_publishable_check is NOT VALID but enforced on UPDATE, so the media_versions backfill below would abort on
-- versions published before 0019 (no rights statement). It is re-added, unchanged from 0026, once the backfill is done.
ALTER TABLE "media_versions" DROP CONSTRAINT "media_versions_publishable_check";--> statement-breakpoint

